// This fixture is an *authored* illustration of the NDJSON capture schema
// documented in the README ("one JSON conversation per line:
// id, title, turns, source, flags"). NOT copied code or real user data.
// Verified project facts (from README, 2026-06-27, v0.1.3):
//   - Capture: Tampermonkey userscript clicks through every gemini.google.com
//     conversation; streams to gemini_chats.ndjson; ~30-45 min for full
//     history; tab must stay open and in front; resume supported.
//   - Guards: content-identity validation (URL id + first prompt must match
//     target and differ from previous), SHA-256 duplicate-body guard, loud
//     failures ("DOM may have changed").
//   - Process: python main.py --verify / --convert / --import-takeout /
//     --reconcile against Takeout MyActivity.json.
//   - Limitation acknowledged by author: page HTML has no conversation
//     content (Angular SPA); scraper must drive the real logged-in UI.
//   - Timestamps per message: not documented in the capture schema.
// ============================================================================
{"id": "c_abc123", "title": "Help me plan a trip to Japan", "source": "gemini.google.com", "flags": [], "turns": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'm planning a 2-week trip to Japan..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's a suggested itinerary..."}]}
{"id": "c_def456", "title": "Explain recursion", "source": "gemini.google.com", "flags": ["retried"], "turns": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain recursion simply."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Recursion is when a function calls itself..."}]}
